<title>FRANCE: BNP in financing deal with Iranian banks.</title>
<headline>BNP in financing deal with Iranian banks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP) said on Thursday it had signed a $500 million export financing accord with four Iranian banks, the first such deal by a French bank since France's export credit agency resumed guarantees to Iran.</p>
<p>BNP said it signed the deal with Bank Mellat, Bank Melli, Bank Saderat and Bank Tejerat.</p>
<p>The accord is aimed at financing goods and service export contracts. The contracts financed under the deal will have to obtain the preliminary agreement of French export credit agency Coface and the guarantee of the Iranian finance ministry, BNP said in a statement.</p>
</text>
